---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/docs.css";
---

<Base
	title="Privacy policy | Actual Budget Tweaks"
	description="What Actual Budget Tweaks stores, what it sends, and to whom."
>
	<main class="docs center">
		<header class="docs__header stack stack--sm">
			<a href="/" class="docs__back">Back to home</a>
			<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
			<p class="docs__lead">
				Actual Budget Tweaks (ABT) is a browser extension and self-hosted sidecar that adds optional
				features to Actual Budget. It has no servers, no accounts and no analytics. The developer
				never receives your budget data or anything about you.
			</p>
			<p class="docs__updated">Last updated: November 14, 2026</p>
		</header>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Data ABT reads</h2>
			<p>
				ABT's scripts load on every page, since your Actual address is yours to choose. On any other
				site they only compare the page's address with the one you entered in its popup, again if
				either changes, and never read the page. On your Actual address, ABT reads your
				budget through Actual's own interface in the page (accounts, balances, categories,
				transactions and schedules) to show its features, such as live balances in the sidebar.
				Your budget data stays between your browser and your own Actual server.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Data ABT stores</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Your ABT settings, in your browser's extension storage on your device.
				</li>
				<li>
					A copy of those settings in your budget, saved as Actual preferences so
					they follow you to other devices. This copy lives on your own Actual server.
				</li>
				<li>
					Data you create in ABT, such as account icons, category colours,
					account groups and custom themes, stored the same two ways.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				ABT changes your budget only when you take an action that does so, such as renaming an
				account from its sidebar.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Data ABT sends</h2>
			<p>
				ABT contacts these third-party services only to provide a feature you use. None of them
				receive your budget data.
			</p>
			<div class="docs__table-wrap docs__table-wrap--wrap">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>Service</th><th>When</th><th>Data sent</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Google favicon service (t1.gstatic.com)</td>
							<td>You give an account a website icon</td>
							<td>The website address you chose</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>jsDelivr (cdn.jsdelivr.net)</td>
							<td>You pick an emoji icon</td>
							<td>A request for that emoji's image</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>GitHub (raw.githubusercontent.com)</td>
							<td>You browse community themes, or ABT shows its release notes</td>
							<td>A request for the theme or changelog file</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Yahoo Finance (query2.finance.yahoo.com)</td>
							<td>You add a stock widget to the sidebar</td>
							<td>The ticker symbol you entered</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>ExchangeRate-API (api.exchangerate-api.com)</td>
							<td>You use the currency converter</td>
							<td>The currency you convert from</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>
				Like any web request, these services see your IP address and browser details. Their own
				privacy policies apply to those requests.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Limits on what ABT does</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>It does not collect, sell, share or transfer your data to the developer or anyone else.</li>
				<li>It does not use analytics, tracking or advertising.</li>
				<li>It does not read or change any website other than the Actual address you set.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Removing your data</h2>
			<p>
				Uninstalling the extension deletes everything it stored in your browser. The settings copy in
				each budget is a set of Actual preferences prefixed with <code>abt:</code>; it stays in that
				budget file on your server and is not read once ABT is removed.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about this policy can be raised on
				<a href="https://github.com/aelxxs/actual-budget-tweaks/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
					>GitHub</a
				>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</main>
</Base>
